Fixed 4 bugs in the ETL pipeline Makefile:

1. BUG #1: Changed $$@ to $@ in the pattern rule (clean/%.csv)
   - $$@ without .SECONDEXPANSION was treated as literal text
   - Now correctly expands to the target filename

2. BUG #2: Replaced $(wildcard clean/*.csv) with $(CLEAN_TARGETS)
   - wildcard is evaluated at parse time, causing stale dependencies
   - CLEAN_TARGETS properly tracks dependencies on source files

3. BUG #3: Made clean/manifest.txt depend on $(CLEAN_TARGETS)
   - Added clean/manifest.txt as dependency to joined.csv
   - Fixes race condition with -j4 parallel builds

4. BUG #4: Added config/params.yaml as dependency to summary.csv
   - summarize.py reads this file but it was not tracked
   - Now changes to config trigger proper rebuilds

RESULT: Incremental builds now work correctly with -j4 parallelism
No segfaults or hangs on subsequent runs
